xt_delta","text":"yahoo.com/news"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"/biggest-mistake"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"-homeowners-recent"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"-boc-110000184."},{"type":"text_delta","text":"html)\n\nSources: ["},{"type":"text_delta","text":"Globe and Mail]("},{"type":"text_delta","text":"https://www.theglobe"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"andmail.com/investing"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"/markets/inside-the"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"-market/article-how-tod"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"ays-inflation-data-"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"has-moved-markets-"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"and-bets-for-future"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"-boc/),"},{"type":"text_delta","text":" [Yahoo Fin"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"ance Canada](https://"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"ca.finance.yaho"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"o.com/news/bigg"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"est-mistake-home"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"owners-recent-boc"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"-110000184.html)"},{"type":"completed","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"opaque","provider":"anthropic","kind":"thinking","data":{"signature":"","thinking":"","type":"thinking"}},{"type":"text","text":"The Bank of Canada's most recent decision was a 25-basis-point hike on October 28, 2026, to 2.50%. That was its first increase in more than three years. The next policy decision is December 9.\n\n**Latest developments (as of mid-November 2026):**\n- **Inflation:** Canada's annual CPI was 3.1% in October, unchanged from September and slightly softer than the 3.2% economists expected. Excluding energy, CPI rose 2.0%. [Globe and Mail](https://www.theglobeandmail.com/investing/markets/inside-the-market/article-how-todays-inflation-data-has-moved-markets-and-bets-for-future-boc/)\n- **Growth:** The economy was flat in August, the second flat month in a row, and early figures pointed to a 0.1% dip in September. [Yahoo Finance Canada](https://ca.finance.yahoo.com/news/biggest-mistake-homeowners-recent-boc-110000184.html)\n- **Market pricing:** Traders put roughly even odds on another hike on December 9. Markets are fully pricing a quarter-point hike by the January 27, 2027 meeting. [Globe and Mail](https://www.theglobeandmail.com/investing/markets/inside-the-market/article-how-todays-inflation-data-has-moved-markets-and-bets-for-future-boc/)\n- **Economists are split:**\n  - Hold expected: CIBC, Citi, RSM Canada and Capital Economics expect no change in December. CPA Canada's chief economist also says the data doesn't call for another hike.\n  - Hike still possible: KPMG maintains a December hike call, and Scotiabank says the data is \"probably good enough to hike in December.\" Macquarie's base case is January.\n\n**What it means for borrowers:** Big banks raised prime to 4.70% from 4.45%, effective October 29. Prime-linked variable-rate debt got more expensive as a result. [Yahoo Finance Canada](https://ca.finance.yahoo.com/news/biggest-mistake-homeowners-recent-boc-110000184.html)\n\nSources: [Globe and Mail](https://www.theglobeandmail.com/investing/markets/inside-the-market/article-how-todays-inflation-data-has-moved-markets-and-bets-for-future-boc/), [Yahoo Finance Canada](https://ca.finance.yahoo.com/news/biggest-mistake-homeowners-recent-boc-110000184.html)"}]},"stop_reason":"end_turn","usage":{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":897,"cache_read_input_tokens":6578,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6877},"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","refusal_category":null}]}
